WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:02.563
- You see this world in New York City,

00:00:02.563 --> 00:00:05.068
and it just seems like Shangri-La.

00:00:05.068 --> 00:00:07.850
It sparkles and glows, and it's just full

00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.561
of this endless potential.

00:00:10.561 --> 00:00:11.894
But also, you know, oh hi!

00:00:13.609 --> 00:00:14.776
Whatcha doing?

00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:21.271
I'm Desi Delong, I'm a
metalsmith in New York City,

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.104
and this is my studio.

00:00:28.107 --> 00:00:29.927
Metalsmithing became a passion for me

00:00:29.927 --> 00:00:32.927
the second I struck hammer to anvil.

00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:49.125
It's extremely important
for me to have a vehicle

00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:50.577
in this city.

00:00:50.577 --> 00:00:52.957
It's a Subaru Impreza.

00:00:52.957 --> 00:00:54.655
I use it to pick up equipment.

00:00:54.655 --> 00:00:56.774
I drive every morning to my studio.

00:00:56.774 --> 00:01:00.358
I also use it to travel
to and from my shows

00:01:00.358 --> 00:01:04.105
up and down the east coast
that are 10 to 12 hour drives.

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:05.662
This car is just along for the ride,

00:01:05.662 --> 00:01:10.018
and I've been on a pretty
crazy ride the past six years.

00:01:10.018 --> 00:01:12.855
The life I had before moving to New York,

00:01:12.855 --> 00:01:15.461
I had a full-time job at Duke University

00:01:15.461 --> 00:01:17.825
as a nurse in the ICU.

00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:20.515
I had a beautiful little crossman home.

00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:24.182
I had found that I was
completely apathetic,

00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:27.726
just passionless, and I wanted a change,

00:01:27.726 --> 00:01:30.354
and I wanted something that felt foreign.

00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:32.292
I wanted to be uncomfortable.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:34.042
I wanted a challenge.

00:01:34.885 --> 00:01:38.315
I realized I had to get
back to my first love

00:01:38.315 --> 00:01:39.648
which is making.

00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:44.074
I didn't even really
think about how difficult,

00:01:44.074 --> 00:01:48.115
challenging, expensive,
or hard it was going to be

00:01:48.115 --> 00:01:50.514
to learn metalsmithing and
make a living doing it.

00:01:50.514 --> 00:01:53.431
All I thought about was just, do it.

00:02:00.977 --> 00:02:02.305
I chose to move to New York City

00:02:02.305 --> 00:02:05.265
because I wanted to see what
living in a city would do

00:02:05.265 --> 00:02:06.182
to my work.

00:02:07.612 --> 00:02:09.778
I love driving to
galleries that have my work

00:02:09.778 --> 00:02:14.034
so that I can see how
they put it on display.

00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:17.653
What I have in common
with Subaru is creating

00:02:17.653 --> 00:02:19.685
a quality product that you can rely on

00:02:19.685 --> 00:02:24.456
that's going to work and it's
going to serve its purpose.

00:02:24.456 --> 00:02:26.687
I don't wanna put
anything out in the world

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:30.187
unless I'm absolutely passionate about it.

00:02:31.307 --> 00:02:33.827
My past experience as a nurse is intimacy

00:02:33.827 --> 00:02:37.994
with body and form really
influences the pieces that I make,

00:02:38.935 --> 00:02:40.472
because I think about these pieces

00:02:40.472 --> 00:02:44.139
and how are they going
to drape on the body.

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:48.137
My knowledge of anatomy and physicality,

00:02:48.137 --> 00:02:51.970
that's what really influences the designs.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:54.034
I've had a life that's
practical and stable and safe,

00:02:54.034 --> 00:02:58.201
and now I've had a life
that's unstable and risky.

00:02:59.371 --> 00:03:02.292
After experiencing both versions of life,

00:03:02.292 --> 00:03:04.535
I can't really do anything now

00:03:04.535 --> 00:03:07.952
unless I'm absolutely completely engaged.

